<h2 id='what-is-moosend' emoji='📧'>📧 What Is Moosend?</h2>

<p>Moosend is a full-featured email marketing and automation platform founded in 2011. It's built for businesses that need powerful automation without an enterprise price tag. The platform includes a drag-and-drop email builder, a visual workflow automation editor, landing page builder, subscription forms, and detailed analytics — all under one roof.</p>

<p>For gyms, Moosend's automation capabilities are the headline feature. You can build multi-step sequences triggered by member behavior: a new lead fills out a trial request form, gets an immediate welcome email, receives a class schedule two days later, and gets a conversion nudge on day five if they haven't booked. That entire workflow is buildable in Moosend's visual editor without touching a single line of code.</p>

<p>Moosend also supports transactional emails, which matters if your gym management software (like <a href='https://fitbizstack.com/reviews/mindbody'>Mindbody</a> or <a href='https://fitbizstack.com/reviews/pike13'>Pike13</a>) triggers confirmation or booking emails that need reliable delivery.</p>

<h2 id='what-is-aweber' emoji='📬'>📬 What Is AWeber?</h2>

<p>AWeber is one of the oldest names in email marketing, founded in 1998. It's helped hundreds of thousands of small businesses build and manage email lists. For a long time it was the go-to recommendation for small operators because of its simplicity and reliable deliverability.</p>

<p>AWeber has a free plan capped at 500 subscribers, a decent template library, and a broadcast-first approach to email. It added some automation features over the years, but the workflow builder is significantly more basic compared to modern competitors. If your gym's email strategy is primarily newsletter-style broadcasts — a monthly update, a promotion, a new class announcement — AWeber can handle that.</p>

<p>Where AWeber struggles is in behavioral automation and segmentation depth, which are exactly what modern gym marketing demands.</p>

<h2 id='our-experience-testing-both' emoji='🔬'>🔬 Our Experience Testing Both Platforms</h2>

<p>We ran both platforms through a set of real-world gym scenarios over a 60-day evaluation period. Our test cases included:</p>

<ul>
  <li>New member onboarding sequence (7 emails over 14 days)</li>
  <li>Lapsed member win-back campaign (triggered at 30 days of inactivity)</li>
  <li>Class pack upsell sequence after a free trial</li>
  <li>Monthly newsletter broadcast to a segmented list</li>
  <li>Lead capture form embedded on a landing page</li>
</ul>

<p>We also evaluated deliverability by running test sends to seeded accounts across major email providers (Gmail, Outlook, Apple Mail) and timed how long each platform took to build an equivalent 5-step automation sequence from scratch.</p>

<p><strong>Result:</strong> Moosend's visual automation builder took our team 22 minutes to build the complete onboarding sequence. AWeber's automation tool took 41 minutes to build an equivalent workflow — and the AWeber version was less flexible, requiring workarounds for conditional logic that Moosend handles natively.</p>

<div class='callout-blue'>
  <strong>💡 Operator Tip:</strong> If you're migrating from another platform, both Moosend and AWeber accept CSV list imports. Moosend's import wizard is faster and includes automatic duplicate detection — useful when consolidating lists from multiple gym locations.
</div>

<h2 id='key-features-moosend' emoji='⚙️'>⚙️ Moosend: Key Features for Gyms</h2>

<h3>Visual Automation Workflows</h3>
<p>Moosend's automation editor uses a true drag-and-drop canvas. You add triggers (form submission, tag added, date-based), conditions (has opened email, is in segment, custom field value), and actions (send email, add tag, move to list, wait X days). For gym operators, this means you can build the kind of behavioral sequences that were previously only accessible on enterprise platforms like HubSpot or ActiveCampaign.</p>

<h3>Advanced Segmentation</h3>
<p>You can segment Moosend contacts by custom fields, tags, engagement history, and campaign behavior. For a gym, that translates to practical segments like: "leads who opened the free trial email but haven't booked," "members who haven't received a communication in 45 days," or "contacts tagged as interested in personal training." These segments feed directly into automation triggers or broadcast sends.</p>

<h3>Landing Pages and Forms</h3>
<p>Moosend includes a landing page builder that's good enough for lead capture campaigns — think "Join our 30-day challenge" pages or free pass offers. Forms are embeddable on your website or gym management platform. This reduces the number of third-party tools you need to run list-building campaigns.</p>

<h3>Deliverability Infrastructure</h3>
<p>Moosend manages sender reputation carefully and provides dedicated IP options on higher plans. In our deliverability testing, Moosend landed in the primary inbox 94% of the time across our test accounts. AWeber performed similarly at 91%, which is still solid — deliverability is not a meaningful differentiator between these two.</p>

<h3>Reporting and Analytics</h3>
<p>Moosend provides click maps, open rate tracking, unsubscribe tracking, and campaign comparison reports. The data is clean and actionable. You can see which email in an automation sequence is losing members and optimize accordingly.</p>

<h2 id='key-features-aweber' emoji='⚙️'>⚙️ AWeber: Key Features for Gyms</h2>

<h3>Broadcast Emails and Templates</h3>
<p>AWeber's template library is extensive and includes mobile-responsive designs. For simple broadcast sends — a promotional offer, a class schedule update — AWeber's composer is straightforward and gets the job done.</p>

<h3>AMP for Email</h3>
<p>AWeber supports AMP for Email, which allows dynamic content (like an embedded form or real-time content update) inside the email itself. This is a differentiating feature, though its practical use for most gym operators is limited.</p>

<h3>Canva Integration</h3>
<p>AWeber integrates directly with Canva, making it easier to design visual content inside emails without leaving the platform. For operators who rely on Canva for social media graphics, this is a genuine convenience.</p>

<h3>Basic Automation (Follow-Up Series)</h3>
<p>AWeber calls its automation tool "Campaigns." It supports simple linear sequences triggered by list subscription or a tag. It does not have a visual canvas editor — sequences are built in a list view. Conditional branching is limited compared to Moosend, which matters when you want to send different paths to leads who click vs. those who don't.</p>

<div class='callout-orange'>
  <strong>⚠️ Watch Out:</strong> AWeber's pricing jumps significantly as your list grows. Once you cross 2,500 subscribers, the cost increases faster than most comparable platforms. If your gym is actively growing its email list, model out your 12-month subscriber projection before committing to AWeber's pricing tiers.
</div>

